                <h1 class="as_heading">Baglamukhi Temple, Kangra</h1>
                <p>Baglamukhi Temple, located in the Kangra district of Himachal Pradesh, is a significant Hindu temple dedicated to the goddess Baglamukhi, one of the ten Mahavidyas (Great Wisdom goddesses). It's considered a Sidha Peetha, a place of divine power, and a Shakti Peetha, a place where a part of Goddess Sati's body fell during its division by Vishnu.</p>
                <p>The temple also features a Havan Kund, a sacred fire pit, where it is believed that Lord Ram himself performed a havan (ritual fire offering) during his time.</p>
